0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"prose prose-neutral max-w-none card p-8","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-primary-600","children":"Personal finance guide"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-neutral-900 mt-2","children":"Mutual Fund Investing Guide India"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed","children":"Understand SIP, lumpsum, CAGR, XIRR, risk, taxation, and goal-based mutual fund investing."}],[["$","section","Match fund category to time horizon",{"className":"mt-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 mb-4","children":"Match fund category to time horizon"}],[["$","p","Equity funds are generally better suited for long-term goals because short-term returns can be volatile. Debt or hybrid options may be more suitable for shorter goals, depending on risk and liquidity needs.",{"className":"text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Equity funds are generally better suited for long-term goals because short-term returns can be volatile. Debt or hybrid options may be more suitable for shorter goals, depending on risk and liquidity needs."}],["$","p","Avoid choosing funds only by last-year return. Fund category, risk, expense ratio, portfolio style, and consistency matter more.",{"className":"text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Avoid choosing funds only by last-year return. Fund category, risk, expense ratio, portfolio style, and consistency matter more."}]]]}],["$","section","CAGR and XIRR answer different questions",{"className":"mt-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-900 mb-4","children":"CAGR and XIRR answer different questions"}],[["$","p","CAGR helps understand annualized growth of a single investment over time. XIRR is more useful when there are multiple cash flows, such as SIPs or withdrawals.",{"className":"text-n